  heroes  tui.Buffer, tui.Cell, tui.blank, tui.cell_at, tui.to_lines, tui.new_buffer
  go      tcell's Screen under tview.Application.SetScreen, tview.Box.Draw
  rust    ratatui::buffer::Buffer, ratatui::buffer::Cell, Buffer::empty, Buffer::filled, Buffer::with_lines, Buffer::area, Buffer::content, Buffer::cell, Buffer::cell_mut, Buffer::get, Buffer::get_mut, Buffer::index_of, Buffer::pos_of, Buffer::resize, Buffer::reset, Cell::new, Cell::symbol, Cell::set_symbol, Cell::set_char, Cell::style, Cell::set_style, Cell::set_fg, Cell::set_bg, Cell::reset, Cell::set_skip, Cell::set_diff_option, Cell::merge_symbol, ratatui::backend::TestBackend
  python  textual.strip.Strip, rich.segment.Segment, textual.App.export_screenshot, textual.App.save_screenshot, textual.App.run_test
  note    a cell covered by a wide character holds "" where `ratatui`'s holds " ", so `to_lines` reads as the screen shows; a buffer is made anew each frame, so `resize` and `reset` are `blank`; a buffer is its own test backend, so a drawing is tested with no terminal

