capability tui/size  the screen's size, and told when it changes
  heroes  tui.area_of, tui.Event.resized
  go      bubbletea.WindowSize, bubbletea.WindowSizeMsg
  rust    Terminal::size, Terminal::autoresize, Terminal::resize, ratatui::backend::WindowSize
  python  textual.events.Resize, textual.App.size
  note    the size is asked of the system while an event is awaited, every 50 ms, so a change comes as `.resized` on Windows too, where no signal tells it; pixels, which few terminals report, are not read. On Darwin `term`'s key reader cannot wait a limited time on a terminal (`hero_term.c` waits with `poll(2)`, which answers POLLNVAL for a device there, measured 2026-11-18 in a pseudo-terminal), so a new size is told with the next key until that is repaired. Repaired 2026-11-19 in `term` (its block term/read-key-timeout: poll, and select(2) where poll answers POLLNVAL); measured 2026-11-20 in an 80x24 pseudo-terminal on this Mac, `read_event_within(200)` with no key sent ended `timeout` after 209 to 217 ms in five runs, so a new size is told within the 50 ms on Darwin too

