  python  textual.widgets.Static, textual.widgets.Label, textual.widgets.Log, textual.widgets.RichLog, textual.containers.VerticalScroll
  note    `ratatui`'s answers held where words are a space apart. Its wrapper answers otherwise where spaces run: it began a line with an empty row for spaces wider than the area under `trim`, and broke `cd` across two rows though it fit on one (`ab    cd` in 3 cells, `trim` false); this package takes the spaces at a break away and breaks no word that fits a row. `ratatui` did not scroll across a centred or right-aligned line, nor across a wide character at the cut; this package scrolls every line, the uncovered half of a wide character a blank cell. A paragraph's widest line is `width_of` over its lines

