dropped
  go      bubbletea.Model, bubbletea.Cmd, bubbletea.Batch, bubbletea.BatchMsg, bubbletea.Sequence, bubbletea.Sequentially (an Elm runtime's messages and commands, which the program's own loop is here); bubbletea.Interrupt, bubbletea.InterruptMsg (Ctrl-C is a key in the raw mode); bubbletea.LogToFile, bubbletea.LogToFileWith, bubbletea.LogOptionsSetter (`log`'s); bubbletea.ProgramOption, bubbletea.WithContext, bubbletea.WithEnvironment, bubbletea.WithFilter, bubbletea.WithFPS, bubbletea.WithInput, bubbletea.WithInputTTY, bubbletea.WithOutput, bubbletea.WithANSICompressor, bubbletea.WithoutCatchPanics, bubbletea.WithoutRenderer, bubbletea.WithoutSignalHandler, bubbletea.WithoutSignals, bubbletea.Program.Send (a runtime's settings and its message queue, which a loop that reads and draws needs none of); bubbletea.ScrollUp, bubbletea.ScrollDown, bubbletea.SyncScrollArea, bubbletea.ClearScrollArea (a renderer's scrolling regions, deprecated by bubbletea); tview.Application.SetFocus, tview.Application.GetFocus, tview.Primitive, tview.Box.Focus, tview.Box.Blur, tview.Box.HasFocus, tview.Box.SetFocusFunc, tview.Box.SetBlurFunc, tview.Application.SetRoot, tview.Application.ResizeToFullScreen, tview.Box.SetDrawFunc's subclassing (DrawForSubclass), tview.Application.SetClipboard, tview.Application.GetClipboardText (a retained tree of widgets with focus, callbacks and a root; in immediate mode the program knows which of its areas has the keys); every Set*Func of every tview widget (SetChangedFunc, SetSelectedFunc, SetDoneFunc and their kin: callbacks, which the language's functions without closures cannot carry state into)
  rust    ratatui::backend::Backend, ratatui::backend::ClearType, ratatui::backend::FromCrossterm, ratatui::backend::IntoCrossterm (a backend behind an interface, the language having none: the terminal here is the program's own, through `term`); ratatui::style::palette::material and ::tailwind and their palettes (colour constants a program writes as `term.Color.rgb`); ratatui::style::ParseColorError and Color's `FromStr` (a colour named by text); every `Stylize` shortcut (`red`, `on_blue`, `bold`, `not_bold` and their kin on Style, Span, Line, Text and every widget: `term.with_foreground`, `term.with_background`, `term.with_attribute`); ratatui::text::Masked (a span shown masked, which `tui.Input.mask` does for the one place it is needed); assert_buffer_eq (a macro: a test compares `to_lines`); the `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `Eq`, `Hash`, `From` and `Into` implementations of every type (the language copies, compares and prints values itself)
  python  textual's DOM, CSS engine, reactive attributes, message pump, workers, command palette, themes, notifications, screens and modes, actions and bindings machinery, animation, `App.run_test`'s pilot, and `App`'s other 200 public names read by `dir()` (a retained-mode framework's machinery: here the program keeps its state, draws it and reads its keys)
